gmeow:stage-export-glossary
    a gmeow:PipelineStage ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/pipeline> ;
    rdfs:label "export: glossary"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Emit the committed per-slice terminology glossary projections: the human-readable Markdown table (generated/catalog/glossary.md, grouped by slice then language with one row per reviewed source→target crossing) plus the two external terminology-interchange lowerings (Principle 17) — the OntoLex vartrans:translation Turtle (generated/projections/glossary.vartrans.ttl: one vartrans:Translation per crossing over the reused ontolex:LexicalSense structure) and the TBX ISO-30042 termbase (generated/projections/glossary.tbx: one termEntry per concept, one langSet per language). All three are derived from the SAME reviewed `.po` entry list the corpus folds (crate::stages::lang_glossary::build_entries) — lossy sanctioned projections, never a second parse, so they cannot drift from the graph; each lowering's honest drop list rides its lang:ProjectionEmission record in graph/lang-projection-corpus. A source-reading leaf like gmeow:stage-export-matrix: it reads the authored `.po` catalogs and homograph declarations directly. The `.vartrans.ttl` is RDF, so it rides as the canonical fold of the RDF-fanout named graph graph/fanout/projections/glossary.vartrans.ttl (attached by gmeow:stage-snapshot, reconstructed byte-for-byte by the superset gate); the non-RDF `.md` table and `.tbx` termbase are opaque byte projections and ride the lang-projections-archive rep with the rest of the lang: deliverable family, tarred by gmeow:stage-archive-blobs off this leaf's product, because a rep is the unit a gmeow:CompressionDictionary primes and these two carry the natural-language term inventory gmeow:dictGmeowLangAstV1 is trained on."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    logic:precondition gmeow:stageInputsAvailable ;
    logic:capability gmeow:stageExecutorCapability ;
    gmeow:stageImpl "glossary" ;
    gmeow:producesFormat "markdown" .

gmeow:stage-export-skos-surface
    a gmeow:PipelineStage ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/pipeline> ;
    rdfs:label "export: skos surface"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Emit the generated SKOS concept-scheme surface (generated/skos/gmeow-skos.ttl): a projection of the lifted logic: NodeKind::Annotation axioms (rdfs:label/comment and skos:definition/prefLabel/altLabel/scopeNote on every GMEOW-authored term), grouped under one skos:ConceptScheme. This is the outbound face of logic: isSupersetOf SKOS/RDFS — the annotation surface is authored once atop RDF 1.2, lifted into the canonical IR, and projected back out here rather than authored as a second source. A source-reading leaf like gmeow:stage-export-glossary: it reads the authored slice modules directly (through the annotation lift), consuming no upstream product. The RDF `.ttl` rides as the canonical fold of the RDF-fanout named graph graph/fanout/skos/gmeow-skos.ttl (attached by gmeow:stage-snapshot, reconstructed byte-for-byte by the superset gate)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    logic:precondition gmeow:stageInputsAvailable ;
    logic:capability gmeow:stageExecutorCapability ;
    gmeow:stageImpl "skos_surface" ;
    gmeow:producesFormat "skos" .

